    {
      "component": "Doctor candidate handoff lifetime",
      "findings": [
        "Ordinary schema 1 retains the 90-second ceiling. Doctor schema 2 uses 1800 seconds only after typed owner admission.",
        "Expiry remains the minimum of selected ceiling, original admitted deadline, source-broker owner deadline and descriptor expiry; issuing or revalidating a handoff does not renew the original deadline.",
        "The worker independently enforces the versioned interval and original deadline/descriptor bounds, then validates full Doctor projection, policy identity/deadline and source inventory before checking the clock again.",
        "A schema label alone cannot obtain Doctor continuation: source and policy joins remain required.",
        "Reviewed regressions exercise actual second-child startup after a 95-second guard-clock advance, source drift, original/descriptor deadline expiry, excessive intervals, future issuance, missing/wrong policy and ordinary-schema spoofing."
      ],
      "status": "accepted"
    },
    {
      "component": "Grok terminal rejection observation",
      "findings": [
        "Schema 3 records only the first terminal rejection using fixed reason/event/field/type vocabularies and bounded counts; arbitrary provider keys, text, identifiers and usage values are excluded.",
        "The closed validator joins the rejection frame strictly after the original terminal and within the observed frame count, and joins timestamps, event counts and original terminal reason.",
        "Terminal acceptance behavior and completion authority are unchanged. Usage events remain observations and are never summed into native final usage.",
        "Historical schemas 1 and 2 replay without fabricated rejection data; callback projection remains schema 1.",
        "Reviewed authored parser, actual router subprocess, runner receipt and benchmark-comparison regressions cover diagnostic propagation while preserving unknown native usage and refusing extra raw fields."
      ],
      "status": "accepted"
    }
  ],
